ents were on the way to  the hospital to get chemo but she  wouldn't make it she dies in the  backseat of her dad's taxi  it had become obvious to yumi's parents  and samsung why yumi died but samsung  would never admit it instead yumi's  manager visited her in the hospital  every week and offered to help with  money from the company if he could  samsung's compensation offer five checks  of around a thousand dollars each yumi's  medical bills have already piled up to  fifty thousand dollars when yumi's dad  said it wasn't enough the manager told  him that samsung one of the biggest  companies in the world didn't have any  more money to spare  it would take 11 years of fighting two  finale against one of the most powerful  conglomerates in the world before  samsung would emit any guilts  in 2018 samsung issued an apology to  yumi's family and the families of over a  hundred victims that met a similar fates  they agreed to pay out an 11.6 million  dollar compensation with each family  only getting around a hundred thousand  dollars  according to samsung killing their  workers is only worth around a hundred  thousand dollars that same year the  company ranked in 54 billion dollars in  profits  see in this world those with the most  power can get away with almost anything  power allows you to control politicians  police and even the courts this allows  you to get away with all sorts of crimes  like fraud tax evasion worker abuse and  yes even murder  and in south korea the ones with the  most power aren't the politicians but  those in charge of korea's biggest  conglomerates  [Music]  there's even a ward for powerful  families like this in korea chebos south  korea's untouchable bloodlines  and at the top of all of them is the  samsung dynasty where one out every ten  dollars made in korea is thanks to  samsung for all intents and purposes  samsung is korea as much as korea is  samsung and this gives the heirs to the  samsung dynasty unparalleled power  this is how you 